## 6. Revised 7-Day Day-by-Day Implementation Roadmap

```
Day 1 ───► Scaffolding, Data Contracts, UI Layout Shell (Split: Map + Chat)
Day 2 ───► Verified Live Providers (Open-Meteo Marine + Weather) with Live Status Pipeline
Day 3 ───► Deterministic Risk Engine & Geospatial Geofence Module
Day 4 ───► Multi-Agent Pipeline (Planner -> Weather, Ocean, Geo, Risk -> AI Synthesizer)
Day 5 ───► Interactive Tactical Marine Map (Click-to-inspect, wave vectors, hazard overlays)
Day 6 ───► End-to-End Killer Workflow Integration & Evidence Inspector UI
Day 7 ───► Error Handling, Degraded State Testing, UI Polish & Vercel Deployment Verification
```

### Day 1: Scaffolding, Data Contracts & Layout Shell
- Initialize Next.js with TypeScript and Tailwind.
- Implement unified type contracts (`MarineMetric`, `DataStatus`, `RiskAssessment`, `OceanObservation`, `WeatherObservation`).
- Create responsive tactical layout with top observation status bar, map viewport (left), and AI intelligence pane (right).

### Day 2: Verified Live Providers (Open-Meteo Integration)
- Implement `OpenMeteoMarineProvider` using verified endpoint `https://marine-api.open-meteo.com/v1/marine`.
- Implement `OpenMeteoWeatherProvider` using verified endpoint `https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast`.
- Implement `IncoisPfzProvider` interface with static `DEMO` advisory sample dataset clearly tagged as `DEMO`.
- Build server-side proxy routes with strict error handling and `LIVE` vs `UNAVAILABLE` vs `DEMO` status generation.

### Day 3: Deterministic Risk Engine & Geospatial Layer
- Implement `ORCARiskEngine` with documented Beaufort, wave height, and gust threshold matrices.
- Add Indian coastal ports reference list and Marine Protected Areas GeoJSON.
- Add spatial calculation using Turf.js: Distance to nearest safe port and geofence boundary checks.
- Add automated unit tests for risk score calculations across calm, moderate, and severe weather states.

### Day 4: Multi-Agent Orchestration
- Implement `PlannerAgent` that decomposes user queries and triggers specialized agent tools.
- Implement `WeatherAgent`, `OceanAgent`, `GeospatialAgent`, and `RiskAgent`.
- Wire Gemini server-side tool calling to guarantee the AI uses Risk Engine results as ground truth.

### Day 5: Interactive Tactical Marine Map
- Implement React-Leaflet map with ocean tile layer.
- Render target coordinates pin, wave/wind direction vector icons, port markers, and geofence boundaries.
- Map click interaction: Clicking any coordinate on the ocean triggers real-time data fetch and safety check for that point.

### Day 6: Killer Workflow End-to-End Integration
- Wire the complete query flow: *"Is it safe to venture into the sea tomorrow morning from my selected location?"*
- Build the **Evidence & Source Card** in the chat UI: Collapsible drawer displaying exact API sources, UTC timestamps, raw metric values, units, and `LIVE`/`DEMO`/`UNAVAILABLE` status badges.
- Verify that clicking quick queries updates both chat and map in sync.

### Day 7: Degraded State Validation, Polish & Deployment
- Test edge cases: Network disconnection, inland coordinates, missing wave data (gracefully showing `DATA_UNAVAILABLE`).
- Verify build (`npm run build`) and responsiveness across desktop and mobile.
- Generate walkthrough documentation and deployment instructions.

